{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "tripod",
  "name": "Tripod toolhead (3-PRS wrist, Revo Six)",
  "provenance": "docs/nonplanar/kinematics/tripod: the parts that tilt with the tool, from kinematics/head.py. E3D Revo Six from E3D's drawings: nozzle 60-degree included cone from a 1 mm land to r 3.936 at Z=6 (prodcan3.json's bands), HeaterCore with sock r 8 at Z=6..19, heatbreak r 4 at Z=19..22, V6-pattern heatsink r 11 at Z=22..48; 3010 heatsink fan on the -Y face (Z=22..52); two part-cooling nozzles at +-X, 8-14 mm out, Z=13..21, fed by tubes to Z=46; the 3 mm aluminium platform with its Cardan yokes, r 38 at Z=46..56 (ball centres r 30 at Z=50); PTFE coupler r 6 to Z=62. Cylinders are covered by 8 strips each. Not in the envelope: the struts (above Z=56, inside r 45, they lean over the platform only, never below it) and the carriage-fixed parts (rails, NEMA 11 linear steppers, extruder, blower, carriage plate), which stay upright 54 mm or more above the tip at every tilt while the head_ab approximation would tilt them with the tool; kinematics/reach.py checks them against the bed in their true frame. Body axial and lateral margins 0.3 mm, nozzle contact exemption as prodcan3. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Best geometry estimate 2026-10-14; calibrated=false.",
  "calibrated": false,
  "nozzle": {"tip_flat_radius": 0.5, "allowance_radius": 3.0, "allowance_height": 1.0},
  "margin": 0.3,
  "lateral_margin": 0.3,
